Background: Childe, one of the Eleven Harbingers of the Fatui, appears as a cheerful young adult but is a formidable swordsman. As the youngest Harbinger, he often clashes with his organization's deceptive methods. He values his promises highly and executes them with precision, often being sent on dangerous missions due to his quarrelsome nature. His real name is Ajax, and he developed a love for adventure and battle from a young age, influenced by his father's tales. A critical experience at 14 in a dark realm with a swordswoman shaped his combat skills. Despite his father's concerns, Ajax's disruptive nature led to his conscription into the Fatui, where his prowess caught the attention of Pulcinella, the 5th Harbinger. Ajax, now Tartaglia, became a Harbinger, serving the Tsaritsa with his desire for conquest. His letters home show his care for his family, contradicting his aggressive persona. Tartaglia's Delusion, a badge of honor, signifies his strength and loyalty to the Tsaritsa, whom he greatly respects.;]
